+ * Patch 0291: negronicpufreq_floor=abl|lut (default abl = the 0098 rule). With lut the lowest row of
+ * d1 (A710) and d2 (X2) is row 0 of their EPSS LUT (the table that 0284 prints at boot) instead of the
+ * row ABL left (d1 17, d2 20 = their top rows at boot 0097/0100), so the governor can idle the big
+ * cores at their lowest row and the thermal cap (0280/0283, negroni_cpufreq_cap(0) = the deepest row)
+ * can really lower them. d0 (A510, the boot cluster) keeps its ABL row as the floor in both modes.
+ * Evidence (README-cpufreq.md "Before 0284"): boot 0097 ran d1 row 15 (2342 MHz) and d2 row 14
+ * (2400 MHz), both below their ABL rows, through SpringBoard and Safari without a fault. No boot has
+ * run d1/d2 at their LUT minimum yet: lut is the owner's decision per test image, abl stays the default.
+ * The three checks of 0284 (floor, cap, wr_perf_state) now use dom_min_row[] (ABL row, or 0 with lut). *
  * Boot args: negronicpufreq=0 leaves the clocks alone; negronicpufreq_mhz=N
  * caps each domain at the highest row not above N MHz (default 3200,
  * above every row: the top of each table); a domain is never set below
